  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington delivered a strong day yesterday\u2014up 14% total, with grooming revenue up 20% and transactions up 20% on five active groomers producing $515 per groomer, well above the trailing-30-day baseline of $475. The team is running hot. However, add-on attach rate collapsed to 46% from 67% last week, signaling a real discipline gap in upselling during a high-volume window. That's operational and fixable. Retail also dipped 8%, which warrants a front-of-house check. Month-to-date Port is down 5% in raw dollars, but DOW-adjusted analysis shows the real shortfall is only 6.1%\u2014the calendar mix was unfavorable, not the team's execution. Year-over-year, you're up 37% in revenue and 35% in appointments; this location is performing structurally well.\n\nHicksville is a different story and worth your attention. Yesterday was a major spike\u2014revenue up 137%, transactions up 112%\u2014but that came on only three active groomers producing $287 per groomer, which is 30% below the trailing-30-day baseline of $412. This was a capacity constraint masquerading as a win. More concerning: add-on revenue was zero yesterday, and bather hours remain at zero across the trailing month. MTD Hicksville is up 10% and beating DOW-adjusted expectations by 8.3%, which is excellent, but the zero-add-on pattern and absent bather support suggest you're leaving money on the table and burning out your three groomers. Glen Cove remains dormant at zero scheduled groomer-days through the next week.\n\nPort Washington's 516-customer lapse pool represents $318K in annual reactivation opportunity; Hicksville's 193-customer pool is worth $139K. Both locations show visit-cadence drift in the 160+ and 73+ \"drifting\" buckets\u2014customers stretching out. This is your stealth churn signal. Reorder Bully Sticks and Treat Tables at both locations immediately; Hicksville is short on supplies (dish soap, paper towels, pink bags).\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Port today: 6 groomers, 0 bather hours; tomorrow: 7 groomers, 15 bather hours. Hicksville today: 3 groomers, 0 bathers; tomorrow: 4 groomers, 0 bathers. Next 7 days: Port 36 groomer-days (strong), Hicksville 22 (thin\u2014consider adding 1\u20132 groomer-"
